      <section class="ew-section ew-section--paper" id="mvp">
        <div class="section-intro">
          <div>
            <p class="section-code">06 / The short-term vision</p>
            <h2>One native fx task.<br />A complete evaluation loop.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>The proposed M1 reference is intentionally singular: a pinned Tailwind v4 account-settings app, native fx ACP, one common lint-assisted workflow, and a reviewed design-system skill as the only treatment delta.</p>
        </div>

        <figure class="feature-figure">
          <img src="/img/explainers/eval-workbench/fx-comparison.webp" width="1536" height="1024" alt="Two collaborators run paired samples through identical test frames into observation trays, one of which remains visibly empty." loading="lazy" />
          <figcaption><b>Claim boundary.</b> This is the planned comparison, not a pilot result. The empty tray is the desired behavior when an observation channel is unavailable.</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <div class="task-brief">
          <div class="task-brief__head">
            <span class="state state--next">Proposed M1 task family</span>
            <h3>Improve an account-settings experience without weakening its design system.</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="task-brief__grid">
            <div><small>Requested behavior</small><p>Add a display-name field with validation and save/error states; require accessible confirmation before reset.</p></div>
            <div><small>Baseline</small><p>The same native fx build, model, prompt, repo, lint policy, repair budget, tools, and user-response policy.</p></div>
            <div><small>Treatment</small><p>Only one reviewed, content-addressed design-system skill is added. Loaded guidance is captured—not assumed.</p></div>
            <div><small>Independent outcomes</small><p>Build/browser assertions, rendered intent review, raw diagnostics, source diff, coverage, retries, model usage, elapsed and human time.</p></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="protocol">
          <div class="protocol__rail" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <article><span>U0</span><h3>Understand the baseline</h3><p>One fresh discovery session establishes actual prompt, tools, policy, skill roots, app behavior, capture limits, and the first unresolved questions.</p><b>1 session</b></article>
          <article><span>D</span><h3>Develop both arms</h3><p>Three paired tasks: baseline and skill treatment. The task user answers under a frozen policy; every helper, retry, and missing cell stays in the denominator.</p><b>6 sessions</b></article>
          <article><span>Review</span><h3>Correct the theory</h3><p>The owner reviews findings and meaning. A skill, checker, or criterion change gets its own identity and consequence; nothing rewrites D.</p><b>Human gate</b></article>
          <article><span>C</span><h3>Protected confirmation</h3><p>Three new paired tasks exercise frozen expectations and withheld controls. Same infrastructure, separate inventory, no favorable-case selection.</p><b>6 sessions</b></article>
          <article><span>R01</span><h3>Fresh reuse</h3><p>Run one retained case again through the accepted local pack to prove the lesson survives beyond its originating conversation.</p><b>1 session</b></article>
        </div>

        <div class="criteria-grid">
          <article><span>01</span><h3>Task function</h3><p>Can the user edit, validate, save, recover from error, and confirm a destructive reset?</p></article>
          <article><span>02</span><h3>Design intent</h3><p>Does the interface use permitted components/tokens while preserving declared visual and interaction intent?</p></article>
          <article><span>03</span><h3>Lint behavior</h3><p>Did the effective rules detect intended faults without rejecting legitimate alternatives or becoming inert?</p></article>
          <article><span>04</span><h3>Allowed changes</h3><p>Did the agent stay inside writable paths and avoid weakening policy, tests, protected references, or checks?</p></article>
          <article><span>05</span><h3>Coverage</h3><p>Were all planned cells attempted, outputs collected, cleanup observed, and gaps left explicit?</p></article>
          <article><span>06</span><h3>Effort</h3><p>How many attempts, turns, tokens, elapsed minutes, review minutes, setup interventions, and retries?</p></article>
        </div>
      </section>

