        </figure>

        <div class="future-loop">
          <div><span>1</span><h3>Permit</h3><p>The customer chooses exact excerpts, purpose, destination, retention, and budget.</p></div>
          <div><span>2</span><h3>Propose</h3><p>Edge returns criteria, questions, skill/config diffs, or experiments through typed contracts.</p></div>
          <div><span>3</span><h3>Review</h3><p>A human owner accepts, corrects, or rejects meaning and visible artifacts.</p></div>
          <div><span>4</span><h3>Qualify</h3><p>Independent controls establish where checks and proposals are useful.</p></div>
          <div><span>5</span><h3>Run locally</h3><p>Accepted packs use customer-side execution and native evidence boundaries without Edge.</p></div>
          <div><span>6</span><h3>Learn carefully</h3><p>Later method revisions are judged on useful findings, false alarms, and total human/compute effort.</p></div>
        </div>
      </section>

